{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[G]Looked like a hundred [Em]guns held on [D]me
Hunkered by the [Am]shed, a Detroit [C]general in company
[Em]Calling boy, come [D]out, we have you [C]jailed
Beside the buckshot [Em]door, I stood [D]still
Wondering how the [Am]hell the bastards [C]found me In those hills
# ? words: "In" @0:29
[Em]And clinging to a [D]letter That I wished I'd [C]mail
{end_of_verse}

